# CHAPTER 2: TOOLS AND TECHNOLOGY USED

## 2.1 Technology Stack

FreelanceFlow is built using the MERN stack, a popular technology stack for building modern web applications:

### 2.1.1 Frontend Technologies

**React.js (v18.2.0)**
- A JavaScript library for building user interfaces
- Component-based architecture for reusable UI elements
- Virtual DOM for efficient rendering
- Rich ecosystem with numerous libraries

**Vite (v5.0.0)**
- Next-generation frontend build tool
- Lightning-fast development server
- Hot Module Replacement (HMR)
- Optimized production builds

**React Router (v6.21.0)**
- Client-side routing for single-page applications
- Nested routes for layout management
- Navigation guards for authentication

**Zustand (v4.4.0)**
- Lightweight state management solution
- Simple API with hooks support
- Persist middleware for local storage

**React Hot Toast (v2.4.1)**
- Customizable toast notifications
- Promise-based API for async operations
- Accessible by default

**Axios (v1.6.0)**
- HTTP client for API requests
- Interceptors for request/response handling
- Automatic token refresh

### 2.1.2 Backend Technologies

**Node.js (v20.0.0)**
- JavaScript runtime for server-side development
- Non-blocking I/O for scalable applications
- Rich npm ecosystem

**Express.js (v4.18.0)**
- Minimal and flexible web application framework
- Robust routing system
- Middleware support for request processing

**MongoDB**
- NoSQL document database
- Flexible schema design
- Powerful aggregation framework
- Geospatial queries support

**Mongoose (v8.0.0)**
- MongoDB object modeling for Node.js
- Schema-based solution for data validation
- Middleware support for pre/post hooks

### 2.1.3 Authentication and Security

**JSON Web Tokens (JWT)**
- Stateless authentication mechanism
- Access and refresh token pattern
- Secure token storage

**bcrypt**
- Password hashing algorithm
- Salt rounds for security
- Constant-time comparison

### 2.1.4 Development and Deployment

**Git/GitHub**
- Version control system
- Collaborative development
- Continuous integration ready

**Vercel**
- Frontend deployment platform
- Automatic deployments from GitHub
- Edge network for global performance

**Render**
- Backend deployment platform
- MongoDB Atlas for database hosting
- Auto-scaling capabilities

### 2.2 Software Requirements

| Software | Version | Purpose |
