# CHAPTER 4: SYSTEM DESIGN

## 4.1 System Architecture

FreelanceFlow follows a client-server architecture with a clear separation between frontend and backend:

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        CLIENT (Browser)                       │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │
│  │                   React.js Application               │    │
│  │  ┌─────────┐  ┌──────────┐  ┌─────────────────┐  │    │
│  │  │ Pages   │  │Components│  │ State Management │  │    │
│  │  │         │  │          │  │ (Zustand Store)  │  │    │
│  │  └────┬────┘  └────┬─────┘  └────────┬────────┘  │    │
│  │       └───────────┴───────────────────┘           │    │
│  │                    │                               │    │
│  │            ┌──────▼──────┐                        │    │
│  │            │  API Client │                        │    │
│  │            │   (Axios)   │                        │    │
│  │            └──────┬──────┘                        │    │
│  └───────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┘    │
└──────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────┘
                       │ HTTPS
                       ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                     API SERVER (Render)                      │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │
│  │                  Express.js Server                  │    │
│  │  ┌──────────┐  ┌──────────┐  ┌────────────────┐  │    │
│  │  │  Routes  │  │Middleware│  │ Controllers     │  │    │
│  │  │          │  │(Auth,CORS│  │                │  │    │
│  │  │ /api/v1/ │  │ ,Error)  │  │ - auth         │  │    │
│  │  └────┬─────┘  └──────────┘  │ - clients      │  │    │
│  │       │                      │ - projects     │  │    │
│  │       └──────────────────────│ - invoices     │  │    │
│  │                              │ - ...         │  │    │
│  │                              └───────┬────────┘  │    │
│  │                                      │           │    │
│  │                              ┌───────▼───────┐  │    │
│  │                              │    MongoDB    │  │    │
│  │                              │  (Mongoose)   │  │    │
│  │                              └───────────────┘  │    │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 4.1.1 Architecture Layers

1. **Presentation Layer (Frontend)**
   - React.js components
   - Responsive UI design
   - State management with Zustand

2. **Business Logic Layer (Frontend + Backend)**
   - Form validation
   - Data processing
   - Business rules implementation

3. **Data Access Layer (Backend)**
   - Mongoose models
   - Database operations
   - Query optimization

4. **Infrastructure Layer**
   - MongoDB Atlas (Database)
   - Vercel (Frontend hosting)
   - Render (Backend hosting)

## 4.2 Database Design

### 4.2.1 Entity Relationship Diagram

```
┌──────────┐       ┌──────────┐       ┌──────────┐
│   User   │──────<│  Client  │──────<│ Project  │
└──────────┘       └──────────┘       └──────────┘
      │                  │                  │
      │                  │                  │
      │            ┌─────┴─────┐            │
      │            │           │            │
      │      ┌─────▼─────┐ ┌───▼────┐      │
      │      │  Invoice  │ │Payment │      │
      │      └───────────┘ └────────┘      │
      │
      ├──────────┐       ┌──────────┐
      │   Lead   │───────>│ Contract │
      └──────────┘       └──────────┘
             │
      ┌──────▼──────┐
      │   Contact  │
      └─────────────┘
```

### 4.2.2 MongoDB Collections

**Users Collection**
```javascript
{
  _id: ObjectId,
  name: String,
  email: String (unique),
  password: String (hashed),
  plan: String (enum: 'free', 'pro'),
  settings: {
    currency: String,
    timezone: String,
    businessName: String,
    businessAddress: String,
    gstin: String
  },
  createdAt: Date,
  updatedAt: Date
}
```

**Clients Collection**
```javascript
{
  _id: ObjectId,
  user: ObjectId (ref: User),
  name: String (required),
  email: String,
  phone: String,
  company: String,
  industry: String,
  address: String,
  website: String,
  notes: String,
  status: String (enum: 'active', 'inactive', 'prospect'),
  defaultHourlyRate: Number,
  totalBilled: Number,
  totalPaid: Number,
  createdAt: Date,
  updatedAt: Date
}
```

**Projects Collection**
```javascript
{
  _id: ObjectId,
  user: ObjectId (ref: User),
  client: ObjectId (ref: Client),
  title: String,
  description: String,
  status: String (enum: 'planning', 'active', 'completed', 'cancelled'),
  budget: Number,
  startDate: Date,
  endDate: Date,
  tasks: [{
    title: String,
    status: String,
    dueDate: Date
  }],
  createdAt: Date,
  updatedAt: Date
}
```

**Invoices Collection**
```javascript
{
  _id: ObjectId,
  user: ObjectId (ref: User),
  client: ObjectId (ref: Client),
  project: ObjectId (ref: Project),
  invoiceNumber: String,
  items: [{
    description: String,
    quantity: Number,
    rate: Number,
    amount: Number
  }],
  subtotal: Number,
  taxRate: Number,
  taxAmount: Number,
  total: Number,
  status: String (enum: 'draft', 'sent', 'paid', 'overdue'),
  dueDate: Date,
  createdAt: Date,
  updatedAt: Date
}
```

